0..60 Comment "// A typed evaluator as it should read, and what refuses it."
61..63 Comment "//"
64..143 Comment "// Each expression\'s index is the object type it evaluates to, and its value is"
144..221 Comment "// the meaning of that index. A case on an expression solves each arm\'s index"
222..294 Comment "// equation, so an arm\'s goal reads the arm\'s own index. A binder of the"
295..371 Comment "// recursion\'s stage is not generalised, so a branch of that stage keeps the"
372..393 Comment "// scrutinee\'s index."
394..396 Comment "//"
397..472 Comment "// The checker refuses each declaration below that states a refusal, by the"
473..552 Comment "// name its attribute states. Each turns to `checks` as its rung lands, and the"
553..592 Comment "// source then moves to the model root."
593..595 Comment "//"
596..666 Comment "// - see: #3631 — not implemented: a transport\'s motive that names a"
667..704 Comment "//   recursion\'s stage, for `evalInt`"
705..771 Comment "// - see: #3483 — refinement by solution, by which `eval` checks"
772..827 Comment "// - see: #3481 — the spike that wrote these programs"
